{"kind":"request","text":"Planner: round eight, and it is two textual corrections. Both are mine, and the first is a shape I have not hit before on this lane.\n\nTHE PROVENANCE LINE WAS A STALE MEASUREMENT, NOT AN UNQUALIFIED CLAIM. My artifacts say \"base equals current main c679fb73\". I verified: main and origin/main are both 3a5d952c, and c679fb73 is this branch's merge-base with main. That sentence was true when I first wrote it several heads ago, and I carried it through four republications without re-deriving it. So the defect is not overstatement this time — it is a measured value restated long after the measurement, in a header that looks like boilerplate and is actually a claim about right now.\n\nThe general form is worth having in the conditions rather than just in my head: the head, the tree and the branch are pinned by the commit and survive being carried forward. The base is not, because it is a relationship between two things that both move. I have written the conditions to say that.\n\nTHE COMMENT FINDING IS THE SIXTH INSTANCE AND CODEX IS RIGHT THAT IT NEEDS ITS OWN ROW. Two comment openings in internal/app assert absolutely and narrow to Unix several paragraphs later. Round seven's conditions swept the seven artifact texts and the three named documentation pages; these were in neither set. Editing them under that request would be me deciding my own scope, which is the thing this lane has spent seven rounds not doing. I have also asked for a sweep of the rest of internal/app and its tests for the same shape, because codex named the two he found and the habit does not stop at the boundary of what a reviewer happened to open.\n\nONE OBSERVATION ABOUT THE BOARD, not a request. Codex withdrew verdict 5f2689dc and replaced it with a9188c85. The replacement is world-stale and the withdrawn one is not, so an actor sorting by staleness would take the retired verdict as current. I ratified a9188c85 because it is the live record and its staleness is ordinary